# inc-4trf: highlight the cheetah in the Wild Shape menu and dump the screen,
# so the monster's description (built by Monster::Describe -> FeatName) can be
# read. Before the fix the description carries a "---103 (below 102 = Dance of
# Tukima)---" debug fallback; after, only real feat names.
#
# The menu is MENU_DESC, so the description pane shows the highlighted entry.
# @cursorto moves the cursor by name WITHOUT selecting, so the menu stays open
# and the description can be photographed.
#
# Real Wild Shape (src/Skills.cpp:5615) from a LOADED druid, so the character is
# fixed. The fixture is a Druid 1; the wizard-switch and Genocide prefix (copied
# from tools/keys/wildshape-gray.keys, which reaches a Druid 3 the same way)
# brings it to the three druid levels Wild Shape needs.
#
# Run through tools/check_wildshape_cheetah_desc.sh, or:
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/druid-shoulder-metal-seed7-opt0822.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/wildshape-cheetah-desc.keys <seed>
@dump:arrival
w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE DOWN DOWN SPACE
ESC
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
d
G
a
a
ESC
@dump:druid3
u
@choose "Wild Shape"
@dump:wildshape-menu
@cursorto "cheetah" DOWN
@dump:cheetah-desc
ESC
@dump:after-esc
